IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lhl-dates`
IMPORT `lhl-rules`
IMPORT `lhl-seat`

-- Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (Vic) -- worked cases for the provider's questions (lhl-seat.l4) and the date helpers
-- (lhl-dates.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's
-- output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

-- Short names for the choices.
`recruitment` MEANS `a business of providing recruitment or placement services`
`contractor management` MEANS `a business of providing contractor management services`
`other business` MEANS `another business`
`supply` MEANS `wholly or principally the supply of labour`
`placing` MEANS `wholly or principally recruiting or placing individuals to perform labour for the other person`
`other character` MEANS `something else`
`9(1)` MEANS `a provider supplies them to others to perform work and must pay them for it`
`9(2)(a)` MEANS `a provider recruits or places them with others who must pay them for the work`
`9(2)(b)` MEANS `a provider recruits them as independent contractors for others and manages their contract performance`
`no head` MEANS `none of these`
`new` MEANS `an application for a licence (s 17)`
`renewal` MEANS `an application to renew a licence (s 28)`
`fit` MEANS `a declaration that each relevant person is a fit and proper person (s 17(4)(a))`
`viable` MEANS `a declaration that the applicant is financially viable (ss 17(4)(ab), 29(1)(da))`
`17(4)(b)` MEANS `a declaration of compliance with the laws in s 23(1A) (s 17(4)(b))`
`23(1)` MEANS `a declaration that the applicant has complied, is complying and will continue to comply with the laws in s 23(1A) (s 23(1))`
`23(2)` MEANS `a declaration that the applicant has a plan to comply with the laws in s 23(2) and can give it on request (s 23(2))`
`23(3)(a)` MEANS `a declaration that the accommodation will meet all applicable minimum accommodation standards (s 23(3)(a))`
`23(3)(b)` MEANS `a declaration that the transport will comply with all applicable transport laws (s 23(3)(b))`
`23(4)` MEANS `a declaration that the applicant made reasonable inquiries about the application and declarations (s 23(4))`
`true and correct` MEANS `a declaration that the information in the application is true and correct (s 17(4)(c), (d))`
`consent` MEANS `the consent of each relevant person to the Authority getting information from third parties (s 17(5))`
`17(5A)` MEANS `an acknowledgement that the Authority may require further information under s 21 or 47 (s 17(5A))`
`28(2)(d)` MEANS `an acknowledgement that the Authority may require further information under s 31 or 47 (s 28(2)(d))`
`29(1)(c)` MEANS `the prescribed declarations, consents and acknowledgements (s 29(1)(c))`
`must grant` MEANS `it must grant or renew the licence (s 24(1), s 29(1))`
`may grant` MEANS `it may grant or renew the licence, being satisfied that is appropriate in all the circumstances (s 24(2), s 29(2))`
`must refuse` MEANS `it must refuse to grant or renew the licence (s 24(3), s 29(3))`
`not yet` MEANS `it must not grant or renew yet: it must first take into account the objection and your response (s 32(4)(a))`
`tier 1` MEANS `a tier 1 business (turnover of no more than $2 000 000)`
`tier 2` MEANS `a tier 2 business (turnover of $2 000 001 to $10 000 000)`
`tier 3` MEANS `a tier 3 business (turnover of more than $10 000 000)`
`no tier` MEANS `none of the three tiers: the turnover falls between the Act's ranges (more than $2 000 000 but less than $2 000 001)`
`Supreme or Magistrates'` MEANS `yes, by the Magistrates' Court or the Supreme Court (s 93(6)(a))`
`Supreme only` MEANS `yes, by the Supreme Court only (s 93(6)(b))`
`s 13 item` MEANS `s 13 providing labour hire services without a licence`
`s 14 item` MEANS `s 14 advertising labour hire services without a licence`
`s 43 item` MEANS `s 43 not notifying changes`
`s 44 item` MEANS `s 44(1) not notifying prescribed changes`
`s 46 item` MEANS `s 46 not producing the licence (offence)`
`s 85 item` MEANS `s 85(2) not allowing a person assisting an inspector access (offence)`
`s 88(2) item` MEANS `s 88(2) assaulting, intimidating or threatening an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)`

§§ `Dates`

-- 12 months after 29 February 2028 is 28 February 2029 (fork F1); 3 years after 1 March 2026 is 1 March 2029; 42 days
-- before 1 March 2027 is 18 January 2027 (Jan 18 to Feb 18 is 31 days, Feb 18 to Mar 1 is 11).
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the date` 3 `years after` (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2029
#ASSERT `the date` (0 MINUS 42) `days after` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 18 1 2027
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 12 2026) `to` (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS 14

§§ `ss 7 to 10 -- do I provide labour hire services`

-- Arguments: business, character, engagement, accommodation, regulations deem, s 10 exclusion, s 11 exclusion.
-- s 7(1): any business, supplying labour, by s 9(1) workers.
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `recruitment` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `contractor management` `supply` `9(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
-- Not in the course of a business; not mainly the supply of labour; workers not within s 9(1).
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `no business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `other business` `other character` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `other business` `supply` `9(2)(a)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `other business` `supply` `no head` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 8(1): a recruitment or placement business placing s 9(2)(a) workers, only with accommodation.
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `recruitment` `placing` `9(2)(a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `recruitment` `placing` `9(2)(a)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `other business` `placing` `9(2)(a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `recruitment` `placing` `9(2)(b)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 8(2): a contractor management business with s 9(2)(b) contractors; accommodation not needed.
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `contractor management` `placing` `9(2)(b)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `contractor management` `placing` `9(2)(a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `contractor management` `supply` `9(2)(b)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- ss 7(3), 8(4): prescribed circumstances; s 10 overrides them ("Despite sections 7 and 8").
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `no business` `other character` `no head` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `no business` `other character` `no head` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- s 10 and s 11 exclusions.
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `other business` `supply` `9(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I provide labour hire services` `contractor management` `placing` `9(2)(b)` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `ss 26, 28, 39, 40 -- is my licence in force`

-- Arguments: hold, start, expiry, cancelled, cancellation day, suspended, renewal applied, day applied, in prescribed
-- period, decided or withdrawn, day decided, day asked. Licence 1 March 2026 to expiry date 1 March 2029.
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 28 2 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The expiry date itself: not in force without a renewal application (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2029) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No licence; suspended (s 39(3)).
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Cancellation taking effect 1 June 2027 (s 40(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 31 5 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2027) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 28(3): renewal applied for on 1 February 2029, in the prescribed period, decided 20 March 2029.
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2029) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 15 3 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2029) TRUE TRUE (`d` 20 3 2029) (`d` 19 3 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2029) TRUE TRUE (`d` 20 3 2029) (`d` 20 3 2029) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not in the prescribed period: no s 28 effect.
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2029) FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 15 3 2029) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 28(4): applied after the expiry date, on 10 March 2029: in force from the expiry date, the gap included (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2029) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 5 3 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 3 2029) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Applied on the expiry date itself: neither s 28(3) nor (4) (finding 3).
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2029) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 3 2029) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my licence in force` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2029) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2029) TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 28 2 2029) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 13, 14 -- without a licence`

#ASSERT `Am I providing labour hire services without a licence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I providing labour hire services without a licence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I providing labour hire services without a licence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I providing labour hire services without a licence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to advertise labour hire services` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I forbidden to advertise labour hire services` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 18 -- barred from applying`

-- Arguments: day wanted, cancelled, day cancelled, at my request, prescribed, refused, day refused, prescribed.
-- Cancellation 15 June 2025: barred to 14 June 2027, free on 15 June 2027 (fork F4).
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 14 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 15 6 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `From what day may I apply` (`d` 1 1 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `d` 15 6 2027
-- At my own request, or in prescribed circumstances: no bar.
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 6 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 1 1 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 6 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Refusal 30 November 2026: the 3 months preceding 28 February 2027 run back to 28 November 2026, so the refusal is
-- inside them and the bar stands; the 3 months preceding 1 March 2027 run back to 1 December 2026, so it is free (fork F4).
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 27 2 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 28 2 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 27 2 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `From what day may I apply` (`d` 1 12 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE EQUALS `d` 1 3 2027
-- Refusal 15 March 2027: no month is short, so free on 15 June 2027.
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 14 6 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `From what day may I apply` (`d` 1 4 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 15 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS `d` 15 6 2027
-- Cancellation 29 February 2028: the 2 years preceding 28 February 2030 run back to 28 February 2028, so it is inside them;
-- free on 1 March 2030.
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 28 2 2030) TRUE (`d` 29 2 2028) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 1 3 2030) TRUE (`d` 29 2 2028) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `From what day may I apply` (`d` 1 1 2030) TRUE (`d` 29 2 2028) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `d` 1 3 2030
-- Both: cancellation 1 January 2026, refusal 1 January 2027; the later bar runs to 31 December 2027.
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 1 2 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `From what day may I apply` (`d` 1 2 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2027) FALSE EQUALS `d` 1 1 2028
-- Nothing in the history: free on the day wanted; a cancellation after that day does not precede it.
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `From what day may I apply` (`d` 1 2 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS `d` 1 2 2027
#ASSERT `Am I barred from applying` (`d` 1 2 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§§ `s 3 -- tiers`

#ASSERT `Which tier is my business` 0 EQUALS `tier 1`
#ASSERT `Which tier is my business` 2000000 EQUALS `tier 1`
#ASSERT `Which tier is my business` 2000000.5 EQUALS `no tier`
#ASSERT `Which tier is my business` 2000001 EQUALS `tier 2`
#ASSERT `Which tier is my business` 10000000 EQUALS `tier 2`
#ASSERT `Which tier is my business` 10000000.01 EQUALS `tier 3`

§§ `ss 17, 23, 28, 29 -- what goes with the application`

#ASSERT `What must go with my application` `new` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS LIST `fit`, `viable`, `17(4)(b)`, `23(1)`, `true and correct`, `consent`, `17(5A)`, `23(3)(a)`, `23(4)`
#ASSERT `What must go with my application` `new` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `fit`, `viable`, `17(4)(b)`, `23(2)`, `true and correct`, `consent`, `17(5A)`, `23(4)`
#ASSERT `What must go with my application` `new` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS LIST `fit`, `viable`, `17(4)(b)`, `23(2)`, `true and correct`, `consent`, `17(5A)`, `23(3)(b)`, `23(4)`
#ASSERT `What must go with my application` `renewal` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS LIST `29(1)(c)`, `viable`, `28(2)(d)`, `23(1)`, `23(3)(a)`, `23(3)(b)`, `23(4)`
#ASSERT `What must go with my application` `renewal` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `29(1)(c)`, `viable`, `28(2)(d)`, `23(4)`

§§ `ss 24, 29, 32(4) -- must the Authority grant`

-- Arguments: information, declarations, not barred, fee, fit and proper, compliance, further information, viable,
-- appropriate anyway, objection, objection taken into account.
#ASSERT `Must the Authority grant my licence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must grant`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority grant my licence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must refuse`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority grant my licence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may grant`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority grant my licence` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `must refuse`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority grant my licence` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `may grant`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority grant my licence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not yet`
#ASSERT `Must the Authority grant my licence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `must grant`

§§ `Dates the provider meets`

-- s 32(3)(b): forwarded 20 December 2026, 14 days to 3 January 2027.
#ASSERT `By when may I respond to the objection` (`d` 20 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 3 1 2027
-- ss 26, 29(7): from 1 March 2026, the last day is 28 February 2029; from 29 February 2028, 27 February 2031 (fork F1).
#ASSERT `What is the last day my licence can be in force` (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `What is the last day my licence can be in force` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 27 2 2031
-- s 34: first in force 1 March 2026; period 1 starts that day, information by 29 March 2026; period 3 starts 1 March
-- 2028, by 29 March 2028. First in force 31 January 2027; period 2 starts 31 January 2028, by 28 February 2028.
#ASSERT `By when must I give my annual information` (`d` 1 3 2026) 1 EQUALS `d` 29 3 2026
#ASSERT `By when must I give my annual information` (`d` 1 3 2026) 3 EQUALS `d` 29 3 2028
#ASSERT `By when must I give my annual information` (`d` 31 1 2027) 2 EQUALS `d` 28 2 2028
-- s 34 duty, period 2 from 1 March 2027, last day 29 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Did I give my annual information in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) 2 TRUE (`d` 29 3 2027) (`d` 1 4 2027) EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `Did I give my annual information in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) 2 TRUE (`d` 30 3 2027) (`d` 1 4 2027) EQUALS `not done in time`
#ASSERT `Did I give my annual information in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) 2 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 29 3 2027) EQUALS `still open`
#ASSERT `Did I give my annual information in time` (`d` 1 3 2026) 2 FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 30 3 2027) EQUALS `not done in time`
-- s 35(1): specified 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `When is my next annual fee due` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 15 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `When is my next annual fee due` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2026
#ASSERT `When is my next annual fee due` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 2 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2027
#ASSERT `When is my next annual fee due` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 10 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2027
#ASSERT `When is my next annual fee due` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 1 3 2027
-- Specified 29 February 2028: anniversaries on 28 February in common years (fork F1).
#ASSERT `When is my next annual fee due` (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `When is my next annual fee due` (`d` 29 2 2028) (`d` 1 3 2029) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2030
-- s 35(2): due 1 March 2027, payable from 18 January 2027.
#ASSERT `From what day may I pay my annual fee` (`d` 1 3 2026) (`d` 10 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 18 1 2027
-- s 42(2)(c): notice given 10 November 2026, response by 24 November 2026.
#ASSERT `By when may I respond to the show cause notice` (`d` 10 11 2026) EQUALS `d` 24 11 2026
-- ss 43, 44: change on 1 October 2026, notice by 31 October 2026.
#ASSERT `Did I notify the change in time` (`d` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`d` 31 10 2026) (`d` 5 11 2026) EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `Did I notify the change in time` (`d` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 11 2026) (`d` 5 11 2026) EQUALS `not done in time`
#ASSERT `Did I notify the change in time` (`d` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 31 10 2026) EQUALS `still open`
#ASSERT `Did I notify the change in time` (`d` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 11 2026) EQUALS `not done in time`
#ASSERT `Did I notify the change in time` (`d` 1 10 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) EQUALS `done in time`

§§ `Inspections`

#ASSERT `Must I show my licence` `an inspector` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I show my licence` `a worker for a provider` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I show my licence` `a host` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I show my licence` `a person prescribed by the regulations` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must I show my licence` `someone else` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must I show my licence` `nobody has asked` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 67(2): ceased 30 June 2027, documents available to 30 June 2033.
#ASSERT `Until when must I keep my documents available` (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS `d` 30 6 2033
-- s 67(4): 14 days from 1 December 2026 is 15 December; 14 December is too short.
#ASSERT `Does the notice give me enough time` (`d` 1 12 2026) (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the notice give me enough time` (`d` 1 12 2026) (`d` 14 12 2026) EQUALS FALSE
-- s 91.
#ASSERT `Can I refuse because it would incriminate me` TRUE `give information or answer questions` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I refuse because it would incriminate me` TRUE `do another thing under Part 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I refuse because it would incriminate me` TRUE `produce a document` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I refuse because it would incriminate me` FALSE `give information or answer questions` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I refuse because it would incriminate me` TRUE `give information or answer questions` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Review and penalties`

#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to refuse to grant a licence (s 24)` `the applicant for the licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to grant a licence (s 24)` `an interested person who objected to the application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to grant a licence (s 24)` `someone else` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to refuse to renew a licence (s 29)` `the applicant for the licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to suspend a licence (s 39)` `the holder of the licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to suspend a licence (s 39)` `an interested person who objected to the application` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to cancel a licence (s 40)` `the applicant for the licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to impose a condition on a licence (s 33)` `the holder of the licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to issue a notice to comply (s 37)` `the holder of the licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to vary a licence (s 38)` `the holder of the licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `a decision to refuse my application to vary a licence (s 38)` `the holder of the licence` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT` `another decision` `the holder of the licence` EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 102(1): notified 5 January 2027, 28 days to 2 February 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` (`d` 5 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 2 2 2027
-- s 94(2) table and the offences.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay` `s 13 item` FALSE EQUALS 800
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay` `s 13 item` TRUE EQUALS 3200
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay` `s 14 item` FALSE EQUALS 200
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay` `s 43 item` FALSE EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay` `s 44 item` TRUE EQUALS 3200
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be ordered to pay` `s 46 item` FALSE EQUALS 12
